---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout title="About — Tamerlan Baimurat" description="About Tamerlan Baimurat: an electrical engineering student connecting trustworthy AI, speech, software systems, and hardware.">
	<header class="page-hero">
		<div class="page-shell page-hero-grid">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
				<h1>Curiosity across the stack.</h1>
				<p class="lede">I like engineering problems where a model, a signal, a user, and a production system all have to work together.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="page-facts">
				<div class="page-fact"><span>Based in</span><strong>Boston, MA</strong></div>
				<div class="page-fact"><span>Degree</span><strong>B.S. Electrical Engineering</strong></div>
				<div class="page-fact"><span>Minor</span><strong>Computer Science</strong></div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</header>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="section-shell content-grid">
			<div class="article-stack">
				<section class="article-section">
					<span class="article-number">01</span>
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">Kazakhstan</p>
						<h2>It started with a keyboard.</h2>
						<p>As a high-school student, I worked with a team on TBZZ-44, an ergonomic split keyboard built with KiCad and adapted firmware. The project placed in the top 40 among 300 Samsung Solve for Tomorrow Kazakhstan teams.</p>
						<p>It taught me that engineering is not a list of technologies. It is deciding what matters, turning an idea into a physical system, and explaining the tradeoffs well enough for other people to understand them.</p>
					</div>
				</section>
				<section class="article-section">
					<span class="article-number">02</span>
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">Michigan State University</p>
						<h2>Software became a way to build quickly.</h2>
						<p>I began in computer science, developed production software and retrieval systems, and taught Python as a course assistant. Software gave me the tools to prototype quickly, but I wanted to understand more of the physical and mathematical system beneath it.</p>
					</div>
				</section>
				<section class="article-section">
					<span class="article-number">03</span>
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">Boston University</p>
						<h2>Electrical engineering connected the layers.</h2>
						<p>Transferring to BU brought signals, DSP, deep learning, speech recognition, digital hardware, and healthcare into the same frame. Today I am most interested in systems that need both technical performance and earned trust.</p>
					</div>
				</section>
				<section class="article-section">
					<span class="article-number">04</span>
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">Outside the lab</p>
						<h2>Guitars, music, and custom keyboards.</h2>
						<p>Speech and signal processing feel natural partly because I care about sound. Away from coursework and code, I play guitar, listen widely, and still enjoy the small mechanical details of custom keyboards.</p>
					</div>
				</section>
			</div>

			<aside>
				<div class="aside-card">
					<p class="eyebrow">Education</p>
					<h2>Boston University</h2>
					<dl>
						<div><dt>Program</dt><dd>B.S. Electrical Engineering</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Minor</dt><dd>Computer Science</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Dates</dt><dd>August 2024 - May 2027</dd></div>
						<div><dt>GPA</dt><dd>3.98/4.00</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Graduate coursework completed</dt><dd>Deep Learning, Human Speech Processing and Recognition, Digital Signal Processing</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Next degree</dt><dd>Planning to pursue an M.S. in Electrical and Computer Engineering</dd></div>
					</dl>
				</div>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-compact">
		<div class="section-shell story-panel">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Compact toolkit</p>
				<h2>Skills connected to real work.</h2>
				<p>The detailed evidence lives in research, projects, and experience rather than in an exhaustive inventory.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="story-steps">
				<div class="story-step"><span>AI</span><strong>PyTorch · TensorFlow · STFT · attention · evaluation · RAG</strong></div>
				<div class="story-step"><span>SW</span><strong>Python · TypeScript · FastAPI · React · PostgreSQL · Docker · AWS</strong></div>
				<div class="story-step"><span>HW</span><strong>Verilog · RTL · FSMs · testbenches · Vivado · Artix-7 · KiCad</strong></div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

